  "routeAdjustment": "Reuse the now proved modular quotient representation for every actual original field element. Native analytic uniqueness and meromorphic-order theorems supply the germs directly. Derive nontriviality by inverting j at a pole or subtracting its finite limit otherwise; no special-value formula or elliptic ramification theorem is needed for this prerequisite. The next normalization can use the same native cyclic valuation ring and existing unit/uniformizer decomposition used for genuine Laurent cusp places.",
  "discharged": "The source ratio evaluation is independent of presentation wherever the denominator is nonzero. Every actual original field element is meromorphic at every upper-half-plane point, and nonzero field elements have finite germ order. Addition and multiplication are preserved on punctured germs; constants are preserved pointwise. The actual order map satisfies the valuation laws, is trivial on nonzero constants, and has a nonzero element of strictly positive finite order at every point, derived from the original transcendental j-coordinate.",
